#Tests

##the whole project is drawn

Every node becomes a dot and every edge a line -- nothing in the graph
is dropped on the way to the screen.

    len(node_dots(STAR_GRAPH, STAR_LAYOUT)) == len(STAR_GRAPH["nodes"])
    len(edge_lines(STAR_GRAPH, STAR_LAYOUT)) == len(STAR_GRAPH["edges"])

##the finale has its edge and its names

The cross-reference the listing shows is a real edge of the graph, and
the opening listing defines enough of the module's names to lift off.

    STAR_GRAPH["edges"][hero_edge(STAR_GRAPH)]["kind"] == "REFERENCES"
    len(liftable(STAR_GRAPH, STAR_LAYOUT, typeset_listing(STAR_MODULE, *OPENING)[1])) >= 5

##every sound is heard in full

With the real numbers of ticks and names, every sound starts after the
teaser begins and has finished before it ends.

    fits(teaser_sounds(sound_counts()), LIMIT)
    sound_counts()["claims"] > 0 and sound_counts()["split"] > 0 and sound_counts()["lifted"] > 0

##the query's answer is in the star module's flower

The address the context beat queried is a node of the star module, with
names of its own beneath it -- the part of the graph the query returned.

    STAR_LAYOUT.cluster_of[ANSWER_ADDRESS] == STAR_CLUSTER
    len(query_nodes(STAR_GRAPH)) >= 3

##every claim on screen is ticked

The results of the real run cover every claim in the excerpt shown.

    every_claim_ticked(STAR_MODULE.read_text(encoding="utf-8"), claim_results(STAR_PROJECT, "petri/marking.lob"), *CLAIMS_EXCERPT)
    every_claim_ticked(STAR_MODULE.read_text(encoding="utf-8"), claim_results(STAR_PROJECT, "petri/marking.lob"), *SPLIT_EXAMPLE)

##the split board is the real net

The board in the split beat is drawn from the net pn-chomper's own code
built, and the chompers end where its firing rule put them.

    split_states(STAR_PROJECT, "petri/marking.lob")["places"] == SPLIT_NET["places"]
    fired_transition(split_states(STAR_PROJECT, "petri/marking.lob"), {"p1": 1}, split_states(STAR_PROJECT, "petri/marking.lob")["after"]) == "t1"

